Install instructions for mc.respond
 by MC_8 - Carl M. Gregory <mc8@purehype.net>
    ________________________________________________ ________ ____ __


1) Edit the file mc.respond.tcl as needed.
2) Add 'source scripts/mc.respond.tcl' to the end of the eggdrop's 
   configs file.
3) '.rehash' (dcc command) the bot.

Done.


Note, the soundex tcl scripts shouldn't be messed with, they are 
automatically called by mc.respond.tcl.



Files:
-----
doc/mc.respond.history                  -> mc.respon's history.
doc/mc.respond.howto                    -> A simple How To on how to 
                                           utalize the script.
doc/mc.respond.syntax                   -> Technical information.
language/mc.respond.croatian.lang       -> Croation language file.
language/mc.respond.dutch.lang          -> Dutch language file.
language/mc.respond.english.lang        -> English language file.
language/mc.respond.french.lang         -> French language file.
language/mc.respond.norsk.lang          -> Norsk (norweagen) language 
                                           file.
scripts/mc.respond.tcl                  -> The main TCL script.
scripts/mc.soundex(Daitch-Mokotoff).tcl -> The Daitch-Mokotoff soundex 
                                           codebase coded specially for 
                                           mc.respond.
scripts/mc.soundex(NARA).tcl            -> The NARA (National Archives 
                                           and Records Administration) 
                                           soundex codebase coded 
                                           specially for mc.respond.
scripts/mc.soundex(NARA+mc).tcl         -> The NARA (National Archives 
                                           and Records Administration), 
                                           plus some modifications by
                                           MC_8, soundex codebase coded 
                                           specially for mc.respond.
text/respond.db                         -> Internal database file used 
                                           by mc.respond.
